hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1273","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya told us, Hisham bin Urwa told us, my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, H. Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Ibn Bishr, Hisham, told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not be careful with your prayers. The rising of the sun, not its setting, for it sets between the horns of Satan.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the visor of the sun comes out, hold back.” abstain from prayer until it is leveled, then if the veil of the sun sets, abstain from prayer until it sets.” This is the hadith of Bundar, and Abu Kurayb said: “It is She appears with the horns of a devil"
"1274","Bundar told us, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sammak, he said: I heard Al-Muhallab bin Abi Sufra, saying: Samurah said: Ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray when the sun rises or when it sets, for it rises between the horns of Satan and sets.” Between the horns of Satan” and in the report of Al-Sanabihi, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The sun rises and with it the horn of Satan, so when it rises So he left her” is an indication that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he forbade prayer at that hour, he also forbade prayer after sunrise until it has risen, Likewise, the report of Amr ibn Absa: Until you rise, I included these two reports in a chapter other than this."
